# One set of line endings, on every machine.
#
# Git for Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout unless told otherwise, and then
# the same file is two different files depending on who cloned it: a test that
# reads a fixture byte for byte passes on a Mac and fails on a PC, a shell script
# grows carriage returns it cannot run with, and a hash of a source file stops
# matching. Text is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree. Git still
# detects binaries by itself; the ones below are named so a false guess is
# impossible for the files where it would be silent and expensive.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.woff2 binary
*.onnx binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
